  data: {
    LLM: 'Game: Tressette. Logic: See rules.objective and rules.gameplay.',
    Player: 'Tressette is one of the great Italian card games. It is a partnership trick-taking game for 4 players using a 40-card Italian deck. The unique ranking (3-2-A high) and the lack of trumps create a pure suit-following game where communication and memory are paramount. There are 11 points per deal.',
    objective: 'Score more points than opponents. Game to 21 (or 31/41).',
    gameplay: '1. Deal 10. 2. Accuso (optional declarations: Napoletana = 3-2-A of same suit = 3pts; 3 or 4 of same honor = pts). 3. Play 10 tricks: Must follow suit. No trumps. Highest of led suit wins. 4. Score: A=1, 3/2/K/Kt/J= 1/3. Last trick=1. Total 11/hand.',
